Code python using scrapy:
url: https://animalcorner.org/animals/

I have <div class="entry-content">....</div>.
Inside there are h2/h3/h4/h5/h6, i dont know how many.
All those heading, hava a class e.q: <h2 class="wp-block-heading">...</h2>, <h3 class="wp-block-heading">...</h3>.
But, sometimes doesnt have class e.q: <h2>...</h2>, <h3>...</h3>.

The main point are:
1. Check how many heading inside <div class="entry-content"></div>, then get all text. Example:
    <div class="entry-content">
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo environment</h2>
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo foods</h2>
        <h3 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo behavior</h3>
        ...
    </div>

2. Check number point 1. If heading doesnt have a class <h2>...</h2>, then get all text. Exmaple:
    <div class="entry-content">
        <h2>buffalo environment</h2>
        <h2>buffalo foods</h2>
        <h3 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo behavior</h3>
        ...
    </div>

That are 2 point, whether heading doesnt hava or have a class, get text.
I know you can do it :)

Can you sparete between heading. Example:
    <div class="entry-content">
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo environment</h2>
            <h3 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo foods</h2>
            <h3 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo behavior</h3>
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo environment</h2>
            <h3 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo behavior</h3>
                <h4 class="wp-block-heading">buffalo behavior</h3>
    </div>

If h2 have a sub heading which is h3, then get text under h2.
also for sub h3 etc.

Example output:

if doesnt have sub heading msg:"No heading again".

